WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.811 --> 00:00:03.213
Sam kiley, CNN, eastern

00:00:03.213 --> 00:00:03.313
Ukraine.

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:04.815
&gt;&gt; Wow, what incredible

00:00:05.215 --> 00:00:05.949
reporting there from Sam kiley

00:00:06.216 --> 00:00:06.883
and his team.

00:00:07.217 --> 00:00:08.785
I want to bring in CNN military

00:00:09.219 --> 00:00:09.953
analyst and retired air force

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:11.922
colonel Cedric Leighton.

00:00:12.789 --> 00:00:13.857
Colonel, thank you so much for

00:00:14.124 --> 00:00:14.891
joining us at this hour.

00:00:15.726 --> 00:00:18.895
What would western supply

00:00:19.229 --> 00:00:20.864
planes mean to Ukraine and its

00:00:21.231 --> 00:00:23.867
ability to push Russia back?

00:00:24.735 --> 00:00:27.771
&gt;&gt; Well, between planes and

00:00:28.038 --> 00:00:29.873
helicopters, you would have a

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:31.742
quite good mix for the

00:00:32.008 --> 00:00:34.811
Ukrainians to actually go after

00:00:35.245 --> 00:00:35.312
the Russians.

00:00:35.579 --> 00:00:37.247
Not only on the front lines but

00:00:37.247 --> 00:00:37.981
behind the front lines.

00:00:38.749 --> 00:00:40.083
So this, is, yeah I think one

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:41.952
of the key factors the

00:00:42.219 --> 00:00:43.253
Ukrainians are still looking

00:00:43.353 --> 00:00:43.820
for.

00:00:44.087 --> 00:00:45.822
One of the key factors that is

00:00:46.089 --> 00:00:47.791
also missing from any type of

00:00:48.058 --> 00:00:50.026
modern military operation.

00:00:50.293 --> 00:00:51.728
Either side has been able to

00:00:51.995 --> 00:00:53.897
declare air supremacy over the

00:00:54.164 --> 00:00:56.099
Ukraine or even air superiority

00:00:56.366 --> 00:00:56.600
over Ukraine.

00:00:56.867 --> 00:00:59.936
And if the uk idiots were able

00:01:00.203 --> 00:01:02.038
to get air support, he even

00:01:02.305 --> 00:01:03.273
into the localized areas, that

00:01:03.473 --> 00:01:04.307
would be a huge deal for them.

00:01:05.275 --> 00:01:06.176
, Now one of the big questions,

00:01:06.910 --> 00:01:08.145
of course, is how well and how

00:01:08.478 --> 00:01:09.913
quickly can they be trained to

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:11.915
use different equipment?

00:01:12.182 --> 00:01:13.850
You know, what Sam shared with

00:01:14.117 --> 00:01:15.285
the M.I.A. Helicopters.

00:01:15.318 --> 00:01:18.121
That is about a two generation

00:01:18.388 --> 00:01:20.857
ago in terms of helicopters and

00:01:21.291 --> 00:01:21.558
aviation.

00:01:21.558 --> 00:01:23.293
If they're going to be brought

00:01:23.293 --> 00:01:24.828
up to speed that is going to be

00:01:25.295 --> 00:01:26.096
a different situation.

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:27.864
And it certainly takes some

00:01:28.131 --> 00:01:28.331
time to do.

00:01:28.598 --> 00:01:29.866
That &gt;&gt; Yeah, there is a lot of

00:01:30.133 --> 00:01:30.834
technology that has been

00:01:31.301 --> 00:01:31.968
majorly updated and a lot of

00:01:32.235 --> 00:01:32.969
things to learn.

00:01:33.837 --> 00:01:35.305
Next week, and I cannot believe

00:01:35.305 --> 00:01:35.372
this.

00:01:35.872 --> 00:01:37.307
But it marks the one year

00:01:37.307 --> 00:01:38.875
anniversary of Russia's

00:01:39.309 --> 00:01:39.476
invasion in Ukraine.

00:01:40.877 --> 00:01:42.813
I remember at the time when it

00:01:43.313 --> 00:01:44.815
first happened that the U.S.

00:01:45.315 --> 00:01:45.882
Intelligence at the time had

00:01:46.149 --> 00:01:48.118
said that probably Russia was

00:01:48.385 --> 00:01:49.586
going to take the capital Kyiv

00:01:49.853 --> 00:01:50.086
in three days.

00:01:52.789 --> 00:01:55.859
That could not have, and of

00:01:56.526 --> 00:01:56.960
course and there have been

00:01:57.327 --> 00:01:58.795
re-thinks of all of, this is

00:01:59.329 --> 00:01:59.763
actually on Russia's side.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:00.864
Did you think the war would be

00:02:01.331 --> 00:02:03.700
where it is today?

00:02:03.967 --> 00:02:04.468
Not knowing what you know now?

00:02:04.734 --> 00:02:08.972
&gt;&gt; Yeah, hindsight is of course

00:02:09.339 --> 00:02:10.207
always 2020, right, Sarah?

00:02:10.941 --> 00:02:13.343
But I think the big takeaway

00:02:13.343 --> 00:02:15.946
here is that the Ukrainians

00:02:16.213 --> 00:02:17.914
confounded most expectations

00:02:18.181 --> 00:02:19.349
they were on the Russian side

00:02:19.416 --> 00:02:20.183
or the Ukrainian side.

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:21.952
Even certainly on the western

00:02:22.219 --> 00:02:22.319
side.

00:02:22.586 --> 00:02:23.353
I think a lot of people

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.990
expected a repeat of 1968 when

00:02:27.357 --> 00:02:28.325
the soviet union and the Warsaw

00:02:28.592 --> 00:02:29.960
pact invaded what was then

00:02:30.227 --> 00:02:32.929
czechoslovakia to get rid of

00:02:33.363 --> 00:02:34.965
that relatively thorough

00:02:35.365 --> 00:02:37.367
communist reform at that point.

00:02:37.901 --> 00:02:39.970
But, you, know Ukraine is quite

00:02:40.237 --> 00:02:40.403
different.

00:02:40.937 --> 00:02:43.373
And Ukraine had tasted freedom.

00:02:43.373 --> 00:02:44.074
They knew that they had to

00:02:44.341 --> 00:02:46.943
fight in order to survive.

00:02:47.377 --> 00:02:49.079
And that's very fact, I think

00:02:49.379 --> 00:02:50.347
it surprised many of us.

00:02:50.914 --> 00:02:52.983
And I think that is the key

00:02:53.383 --> 00:02:53.617
thing.

00:02:53.617 --> 00:02:55.385
It is quite a surprisingly

00:02:55.552 --> 00:02:56.219
thing that they do this.

00:02:56.920 --> 00:02:58.054
Now that we are at this point,

00:02:58.321 --> 00:03:01.391
they need, the Ukrainians need

00:03:01.491 --> 00:03:06.429
a lot more jobs of ammunition

00:03:06.696 --> 00:03:08.298
and the ability to actually

00:03:08.565 --> 00:03:09.533
regain the territory they've

00:03:09.799 --> 00:03:09.900
lost.

00:03:10.166 --> 00:03:11.401
They've done a major job in

00:03:11.601 --> 00:03:12.569
recapture in a lot of territory

00:03:13.403 --> 00:03:13.537
up to this point.

00:03:13.803 --> 00:03:15.405
But they haven't quite gotten

00:03:15.672 --> 00:03:17.407
what they want in order to

00:03:17.507 --> 00:03:19.476
achieve that stalemate that

00:03:19.743 --> 00:03:20.110
they are looking for.

00:03:20.377 --> 00:03:21.411
&gt;&gt; Yeah there is still some

00:03:21.545 --> 00:03:22.412
horrible bloody battles.

00:03:22.679 --> 00:03:23.580
They continue and continue to

00:03:23.847 --> 00:03:25.515
take civilians lives.

00:03:26.216 --> 00:03:27.417
One of the things about being

00:03:27.651 --> 00:03:28.351
on the ground there from my

00:03:28.618 --> 00:03:30.520
perspective is there were a few

00:03:30.787 --> 00:03:33.423
things that really changed the

00:03:33.557 --> 00:03:34.457
tenor and tone of this.

00:03:34.724 --> 00:03:35.592
One of them was zelenskyy.

00:03:36.226 --> 00:03:37.427
Him staying in place.

00:03:37.594 --> 00:03:39.429
Him fighting back himself.

00:03:39.529 --> 00:03:42.566
And not just putting his

00:03:42.832 --> 00:03:44.367
countryman in front, on the

00:03:44.634 --> 00:03:44.834
front line.

00:03:45.435 --> 00:03:46.436
The other is that the Ukrainian

00:03:46.703 --> 00:03:47.437
people aren't having.

00:03:47.537 --> 00:03:49.439
It, like you talk about his

00:03:49.506 --> 00:03:50.173
grandmother's, to grandbabies?

00:03:50.440 --> 00:03:50.473
.

00:03:51.441 --> 00:03:52.441
--

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:59.449
the U.S. Has been warning its

00:03:59.516 --> 00:04:01.985
allies that China may increase

00:04:02.252 --> 00:04:04.020
its military support of

00:04:04.287 --> 00:04:04.421
Ukraine.

00:04:04.988 --> 00:04:07.123
And what that would mean.

00:04:07.991 --> 00:04:09.125
I would like to hear from you

00:04:09.459 --> 00:04:10.193
what do you think that would

00:04:10.460 --> 00:04:12.128
mean, if China decides to start

00:04:12.395 --> 00:04:15.465
supplying Russia with whatever

00:04:15.465 --> 00:04:16.232
it may need.

00:04:17.033 --> 00:04:18.101
Although everyone thought that

00:04:18.368 --> 00:04:19.469
Russia's forces were stronger

00:04:19.536 --> 00:04:20.270
than Ukraine's.

00:04:21.037 --> 00:04:22.806
But what would that mean going

00:04:23.073 --> 00:04:23.473
forward for Ukraine?

00:04:23.673 --> 00:04:28.044
&gt;&gt; Yeah, certainly we would

00:04:28.311 --> 00:04:30.080
have some problems for Ukraine.

00:04:30.347 --> 00:04:31.481
I think one of the key things

00:04:31.514 --> 00:04:33.984
to think about here is the huge

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:35.485
disparity in terms of numbers

00:04:35.552 --> 00:04:36.920
between the Ukrainians and the

00:04:37.487 --> 00:04:37.621
Russians.

00:04:37.621 --> 00:04:39.990
The Russians about --

00:04:40.957 --> 00:04:44.294
ten times the defense budget of

00:04:44.561 --> 00:04:44.828
the Ukrainians.

00:04:45.095 --> 00:04:46.896
And, that you, know was also

00:04:47.163 --> 00:04:48.098
reflected in personnel numbers.

00:04:48.365 --> 00:04:50.033
But what we have learned since

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:52.168
then is that the quantitative

00:04:52.435 --> 00:04:54.971
ability of the Russians and the

00:04:55.505 --> 00:04:56.306
quantitative ponderance of the

00:04:56.573 --> 00:04:59.042
Russians is really not a match

00:04:59.509 --> 00:05:00.310
for the Ukrainians as long as

00:05:00.977 --> 00:05:02.912
the Ukrainians get the weapons

00:05:03.179 --> 00:05:04.114
that they need from the west.

00:05:04.381 --> 00:05:05.982
So the Chinese, if they support

00:05:06.249 --> 00:05:07.951
the Russians, you know, in a

00:05:08.218 --> 00:05:09.919
major way, that is going to put

00:05:10.186 --> 00:05:11.521
a strain on the Ukraine.

00:05:11.521 --> 00:05:12.956
It's also going to put a strain

00:05:13.523 --> 00:05:14.324
on, nato nato will have to step

00:05:14.691 --> 00:05:16.059
up its game, the defense

00:05:16.326 --> 00:05:17.093
industrial base is going to

00:05:17.527 --> 00:05:19.062
have to play a huge part in

00:05:19.529 --> 00:05:20.263
resupplying Ukrainians, and it

00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:22.899
is going to have to do so,

00:05:23.166 --> 00:05:23.533
they're very quickly.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:24.300
We have to expect the Chinese

00:05:24.968 --> 00:05:25.168
to do this.

00:05:25.535 --> 00:05:27.170
But we have to act accordingly.

00:05:27.537 --> 00:05:28.238
&gt;&gt; Okay, this is an unprovoked

00:05:28.505 --> 00:05:30.974
war from the auspices of

00:05:31.541 --> 00:05:32.042
Ukraine side.

00:05:32.042 --> 00:05:34.110
Russia invaded for no apparent

00:05:34.377 --> 00:05:35.545
reason other than wanting to

00:05:35.545 --> 00:05:36.179
take a territory.

00:05:36.446 --> 00:05:37.547
So we will see what happens in

00:05:37.614 --> 00:05:38.014
the end.

00:05:38.281 --> 00:05:40.316
But I know that the Ukrainians

